   ],
   "note": "Text line readers and flushFile open files through the runtime's node:fs/promises and spill streams use node:fs createWriteStream (as upstream), so FileHandle spies and vi.mock(\"node:fs\") reach them; binary readers open natively because pi-jsrt's fs.open has no O_NONBLOCK/O_NOFOLLOW. readTextLines/exists compose this.openTextLineReader/this.fileInfo like upstream. State is held under a module symbol (upstream uses TS private), so Object.create(env) works. No listFiles (upstream NodeExecutionEnv has none at the pin)."
  },
