   "pending": [],
   "note": "Env cases are the native case list run through the caller's provider against the JS env (JsEnv). Storage cases replay the pinned per-backend recordings (crates/pi-durable/tests/fixtures/storage*.json, the traces pi_durable::testing replays natively) through the storage's own JS methods, compared with the caller's expect; the recording follows the storage's class (Memory/Jsonl/Sqlite[Native]/IndexedDb), and a storage holding one (ReopeningStorage) replays that backend's -reopen recording. Verified: memory-storage 27/27, sqlite-storage 65/65, sqlite-cloudflare 30/30, jsonl-storage 91/93 with every conformance case passing (2 Pico failures outside the drivers), both modes. Benchmarks: the reference drivers over the storage's own methods; at load their names, order and write counts are checked against pi_durable::testing::storage_{read,write}_benchmarks, and the scales/record count come from the native definitions. Covered by env_embedded::storage_benchmarks_run_on_memory_and_sqlite (every read and write result equals its expected value on MemoryStorage and SQLite)."
  }
